# A comment above a pattern says why that pattern is ignored.
#
# Until 2026-08-21 this file held thirteen comments stacked at
# the top and fourteen patterns stacked below them, because the
# whole file had been sorted alphabetically at some point. Every
# comment still described something; none of them described the
# line underneath it, which is the only place a reader looks.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.venv/

# selection_ui's own environment, deliberately separate from
# .venv (decision #9, 2026-08-29 — see
# selection_ui/requirements.txt and scripts/setup_selection_ui_env.sh).
.venv-selection-ui/

# priority_ui's own environment, same reasoning, 2026-09-03 — see
# priority_ui/requirements.txt and scripts/setup_priority_ui_env.sh.
.venv-priority-ui/

# Local environment and secrets. Never committed: these carry
# per-machine values, and one of them carries credentials.
.env
.env.selection-ui
.env.priority-ui
.env.resource-priority

# Deployment-specific transfer target. The path a given host
# ships bundles to is a property of that host, not of AIStack.
config/context_bundle_transfer.yml

# Generated artifacts. ENG-P-003: what a pipeline can rebuild is
# disposable, and committing it makes the repository the SPOT of
# a projection rather than of the heritage.
#
# `build/` and `dist/` were absent until 2026-08-22, so
# `python -m build` — the standard packaging command, in a project
# whose ADR-0001 is *Python Packaging v1* — left an untracked build
# tree that any `git add -A` would have committed.
build/
dist/
context/bundles/
reports/generated/
examples/catalog_engine/music-library-catalog.yml
examples/render_engine/*.html

# Wrong path since whatever commit moved this generator's output
# directory from examples/selection_engine/ to examples/selections/
# — the pattern kept naming the old path, matched nothing, and the
# file it was meant to exclude was committed instead. Found live on
# GIGABYTE, 2026-09-03: it kept showing as locally modified and
# blocking OPS-0002's clean-tree gate on every publication. Corrected
# path, plus `git rm --cached` on the file this same commit.
examples/selections/music-android-selection-real.yml

# selection_ui's own materialisation report, one per Application
# Definition — `_last_generation_path` (`selection_ui/app.py`) names
# it `{app_id}-last-generation.yml`, written beside that
# definition's own `selection_file`. Generated on every "générer"
# click (`materialise_by_hardlink`, ENG-P-003 disposable, same as
# the selection file itself). A pattern, not a literal path: found
# live on GIGABYTE, 2026-09-03, as
# `music_android-last-generation.yml` (`app_id: music_android`,
# underscore — `selection_ui/definitions/music_android.yml` already
# names a second instance of the family as the reason this file's
# own shape can change), and the definition anticipates a second
# `app_id` existing later, which would write a second, differently
# named report right beside it.
examples/selections/*-last-generation.yml

# Runtime logs
logs/*.log

# Local backups
*.bak-*

# Patches produced for transfer to another machine.
#
# ENG-P-003: a generated artifact is disposable. A patch is a
# projection of commits that already exist in the history — the
# history is their SPOT, and a patch file in the tree is a second
# copy of knowledge the repository already holds.
#
# Added 2026-08-22 after two of them were written into the working
# tree instead of /tmp, one day after the transit residue of the
# same kind had been cleaned out of `docs/`.
*.patch
patches-*.tar.gz
